There is at least one more very good reason for jumping in a pool of water...

SPOILER WARNING

Obviously, you need to be able to teleport out again immediately, either
via the spell, intrinsic ability, or rings - make sure you can teleport
at will.

First I'll give a hint for those who like to work these things out for
themselves:

It's not much use unless you also have a magic marker.

Think about it.

Ok, consider this.

What happens to your scrolls when they get wet? And just think how much
more wetness there is in a pool compared to a scrappy little fountain.
Why, it might do the lot without even drying up. And no risk of a nasty
water monster appearing.

"they say that 20 blank scrolls and a magic marker is a recipe for success"
